4. Modularize the code:
   Break down the code into smaller, reusable modules. This will improve maintainability and allow you to easily integrate the web service with other components.

5. Ensure interoperability:
   To ensure interoperability, follow industry standards and protocols. For example, use HTTP as the transport protocol and SOAP (Simple Object Access Protocol) as the messaging protocol. Also, ensure that your web service supports common data formats like JSON or CSV.

6. Implement distribution:
   To implement distribution, deploy the web service on a server and make it accessible to clients over the internet. You can use cloud-based hosting services like AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud Platform to host your web service.

