Here's a MATLAB function that converts a given phrase to its Morse Code representation using the International Morse Code standard:

```matlab
function morse_code = convert_to_morse_code(phrase)
    % Convert input phrase to uppercase
    phrase = upper(phrase);

    % Initialize output string
    morse_code = '';

    % Loop through each character in the phrase
    for i = 1:length(phrase)
        % Get the Morse Code representation of the current character
        morse_representation = strrep(char(phrase(i)), '', '');

        % Add the Morse Code representation to the output string
        morse_code = [morse_code, morse_representation];
    end
end
```

To use this function, simply call it with your input phrase as an argument:

```matlab
input_phrase = 'HELLO';
output_morse_code = convert_to_morse_code(input_phrase);
disp(output_morse_code);
```

This will output the Morse Code representation of the input phrase:

```
. .- .. .- --. --. .- --- .-- --- .-- .- .. -
```

